<title>UK: Greece sets second 100 million mark five-year FRN.</title>
<headline>Greece sets second 100 million mark five-year FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following floating-rate issue was announced by lead manager Nomura Bank Frankfurt on Monday.</p>
<p> BORROWER   GREECE</p>
<p> AMT    100 MLN DEM   BASE	 6M-LIBOR  MATURITY    17.JUL.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN     +20 BP    PAY DATE    17.JUL.97</p>
<p> MOODY	BAA1	ISS PRICE  99.91     FULL FEES   0.15</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  BBB-	REOFFER    =	   SALE LIMS US/GB/JP/DE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K) 10</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  GREECE</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.05	SELL CONC  0.10</p>
<p> NOTES	GREECE LAUNCHED A SIMILAR 100 MLN DEM FRN</p>
<p>		EARLIER VIA GOLDMAN SACHS.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
